From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FerrionOS <noreply@ferrionos.invalid>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:34:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] layout: Minimize the windows of a free workspace (F6)

A floating window of a free workspace can be minimized: by the new
`minimize-window` action, by its app through xdg-shell's
set_minimized, and by a dock through wlr-foreign-toplevel. A minimized
window stays a tile of the floating layout, parked: it keeps its place,
its size and every operation on it, but it is not drawn, cannot be hit
by the pointer and never has the focus. Activating it, as focusing it,
the recent-windows switcher and a dock do, brings it back on top where
it was.

- Only floating windows of free workspaces are offered minimize: the
  capability is set on the first configure and kept up to date on each
  refresh, through a new LayoutElement::set_free_state().
- The IPC window record and the foreign-toplevel state say which
  windows are minimized, for the dock.
- Switching a workspace to columns brings its minimized windows back,
  and so does moving one to another workspace.
- With every floating window minimized, a fullscreen or maximized
  window in the columns takes the focus, and so does a window that
  arrives; a minimized window that goes fullscreen or maximized comes
  back focused, and a dialog of a minimized window opens as a new
  window.
- src/ui/mru.rs needs no change: the switcher lists every window of
  the layout and activates its choice.

Agent-written tests and their test-only helpers were removed under ADR 0025.
The source commit in the header records the original patch provenance;
this patch is regenerated against the preceding test-free stage. Upstream
tests remain, with the config snapshots adapted to the production fields.
